@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.971 = private unnamed_addr constant [990 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for a `DAG()` class or `@dag()` decorator without an explicit\0A`schedule` (or `schedule_interval` for Airflow 1) parameter.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe default value of the `schedule` parameter on Airflow 2 and\0A`schedule_interval` on Airflow 1 is `timedelta(days=1)`, which is almost\0Anever what a user is looking for. Airflow 3 changed the default value to `None`,\0Aand would break existing dags using the implicit default.\0A\0AIf your dag does not have an explicit `schedule` / `schedule_interval` argument,\0AAirflow 2 schedules a run for it every day (at the time determined by `start_date`).\0ASuch a dag will no longer be scheduled on Airflow 3 at all, without any\0Aexceptions or other messages visible to the user.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom airflow import DAG\0A\0A\0A# Using the implicit default schedule.\0Adag = DAG(dag_id=\22my_dag\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom datetime import timedelta\0A\0Afrom airflow import DAG\0A\0A\0Adag = DAG(dag_id=\22my_dag\22, schedule=timedelta(days=1))\0A```\0A", align 1
@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.972 = private unnamed_addr constant [47 x i8] c"DAG should have an explicit `schedule` argument", align 1
@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.973 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ ptr, [8 x i8] }> <{ ptr @anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.972, [8 x i8] c"/\00\00\00\00\00\00\00" }>, align 8
@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.974 = private unnamed_addr constant [38 x i8] c"airflow-variable-name-task-id-mismatch", align 1
@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.975 = private unnamed_addr constant [526 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks that the task variable name matches the `task_id` value for\0AAirflow Operators.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AWhen initializing an Airflow Operator, for consistency, the variable\0Aname should match the `task_id` value. This makes it easier to\0Afollow the flow of the DAG.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom airflow.operators import PythonOperator\0A\0A\0Aincorrect_name = PythonOperator(task_id=\22my_task\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom airflow.operators import PythonOperator\0A\0A\0Amy_task = PythonOperator(task_id=\22my_task\22)\0A```\0A", align 1
@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.976 = private unnamed_addr constant [48 x i8] c"Task variable name should match the `task_id`: \22", align 1
@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.977 = private unnamed_addr constant [1 x i8] c"\22", align 1
