@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1005 = private unnamed_addr constant [32 x i8] c"suspicious-insecure-cipher-usage", align 1
@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1006 = private unnamed_addr constant [889 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of weak or broken cryptographic ciphers.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AWeak or broken cryptographic ciphers may be susceptible to attacks that\0Aallow an attacker to decrypt ciphertext without knowing the key or\0Aotherwise compromise the security of the cipher, such as forgeries.\0A\0AUse strong, modern cryptographic ciphers instead of weak or broken ones.\0A\0AIn [preview], this rule will also flag references to insecure ciphers.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives.ciphers import Cipher, algorithms\0A\0Aalgorithm = algorithms.ARC4(key)\0Acipher = Cipher(algorithm, mode=None)\0Aencryptor = cipher.encryptor()\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom cryptography.fernet import Fernet\0A\0Afernet = Fernet(key)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-327](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/327.html)\0A\0A[preview]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/preview/\0A", align 1
@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1007 = private unnamed_addr constant [70 x i8] c"Use of insecure cipher, replace with a known secure cipher such as AES", align 1
@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1008 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ ptr, [8 x i8] }> <{ ptr @anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1007, [8 x i8] c"F\00\00\00\00\00\00\00" }>, align 8
@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1009 = private unnamed_addr constant [37 x i8] c"suspicious-insecure-cipher-mode-usage", align 1
@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1010 = private unnamed_addr constant [1043 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of weak or broken cryptographic cipher modes.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AWeak or broken cryptographic ciphers may be susceptible to attacks that\0Aallow an attacker to decrypt ciphertext without knowing the key or\0Aotherwise compromise the security of the cipher, such as forgeries.\0A\0AUse strong, modern cryptographic ciphers instead of weak or broken ones.\0A\0AIn [preview], this rule will also flag references to insecure cipher modes.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives.ciphers import Cipher, algorithms, modes\0A\0Aalgorithm = algorithms.ARC4(key)\0Acipher = Cipher(algorithm, mode=modes.ECB(iv))\0Aencryptor = cipher.encryptor()\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives.ciphers import Cipher, algorithms, modes\0A\0Aalgorithm = algorithms.ARC4(key)\0Acipher = Cipher(algorithm, mode=modes.CTR(iv))\0Aencryptor = cipher.encryptor()\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-327](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/327.html)\0A\0A[preview]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/preview/\0A", align 1
