@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1033 = private unnamed_addr constant [34 x i8] c"suspicious-xmlc-element-tree-usage", align 1
@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1034 = private unnamed_addr constant [1109 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of insecure XML parsers.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AMany XML parsers are vulnerable to XML attacks (such as entity expansion),\0Awhich cause excessive memory and CPU usage by exploiting recursion. An\0Aattacker could use such methods to access unauthorized resources.\0A\0AConsider using the `defusedxml` package when parsing untrusted XML data,\0Ato protect against XML attacks.\0A\0AIn [preview], this rule will also flag references to insecure XML parsers.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom xml.etree.cElementTree import parse\0A\0Atree = parse(\22untrusted.xml\22)  # Vulnerable to XML attacks.\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom defusedxml.cElementTree import parse\0A\0Atree = parse(\22untrusted.xml\22)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `xml` \E2\80\94 XML processing modules](https://docs.python.org/3/library/xml.html)\0A- [PyPI: `defusedxml`](https://pypi.org/project/defusedxml/)\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-400](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/400.html)\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-776](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/776.html)\0A\0A[preview]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/preview/\0A", align 1
