@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1058 = private unnamed_addr constant [523 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the use of Telnet-related functions.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ATelnet is considered insecure because it does not encrypt data sent over\0Athe connection and is vulnerable to numerous attacks.\0A\0AInstead, consider using a more secure protocol such as SSH.\0A\0AIn [preview], this rule will also flag references to Telnet-related functions.\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `telnetlib` \E2\80\94 Telnet client](https://docs.python.org/3/library/telnetlib.html)\0A\0A[preview]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/preview/\0A", align 1
