@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1066 = private unnamed_addr constant [858 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of the `try`-`except`-`continue` pattern.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `try`-`except`-`continue` pattern suppresses all exceptions.\0ASuppressing exceptions may hide errors that could otherwise reveal\0Aunexpected behavior, security vulnerabilities, or malicious activity.\0AInstead, consider logging the exception.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport logging\0A\0Awhile predicate:\0A    try:\0A        ...\0A    except Exception:\0A        continue\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport logging\0A\0Awhile predicate:\0A    try:\0A        ...\0A    except Exception as exc:\0A        logging.exception(\22Error occurred\22)\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-bandit.check-typed-exception`\0A\0A## References\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-703](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/703.html)\0A- [Python documentation: `logging`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/logging.html)\0A", align 1
