@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1082 = private unnamed_addr constant [513 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for exception handlers that catch an empty tuple.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AAn exception handler that catches an empty tuple will not catch anything,\0Aand is indicative of a mistake. Instead, add exceptions to the `except`\0Aclause.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Atry:\0A    1 / 0\0Aexcept ():\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Atry:\0A    1 / 0\0Aexcept ZeroDivisionError:\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `except` clause](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/compound_stmts.html#except-clause)\0A", align 1
