@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1093 = private unnamed_addr constant [1172 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of mutable objects as `ContextVar` defaults.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A\0AThe `ContextVar` default is evaluated once, when the `ContextVar` is defined.\0A\0AThe same mutable object is then shared across all `.get()` method calls to\0Athe `ContextVar`. If the object is modified, those modifications will persist\0Aacross calls, which can lead to unexpected behavior.\0A\0AInstead, prefer to use immutable data structures. Alternatively, take\0A`None` as a default, and initialize a new mutable object inside for each\0Acall using the `.set()` method.\0A\0ATypes outside the standard library can be marked as immutable with the\0A[`lint.flake8-bugbear.extend-immutable-calls`] configuration option.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom contextvars import ContextVar\0A\0A\0Acv: ContextVar[list] = ContextVar(\22cv\22, default=[])\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom contextvars import ContextVar\0A\0A\0Acv: ContextVar[list | None] = ContextVar(\22cv\22, default=None)\0A\0A...\0A\0Aif cv.get() is None:\0A    cv.set([])\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-bugbear.extend-immutable-calls`\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `contextvars` \E2\80\94 Context Variables](https://docs.python.org/3/library/contextvars.html)\0A", align 1
