@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1102 = private unnamed_addr constant [702 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for unnecessary `dict()`, `list()` or `tuple()` calls that can be\0Arewritten as empty literals.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIt's unnecessary to call, e.g., `dict()` as opposed to using an empty\0Aliteral (`{}`). The former is slower because the name `dict` must be\0Alooked up in the global scope in case it has been rebound.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adict()\0Adict(a=1, b=2)\0Alist()\0Atuple()\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0A{}\0A{\22a\22: 1, \22b\22: 2}\0A[]\0A()\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThis rule's fix is marked as unsafe, as it may occasionally drop comments\0Awhen rewriting the call. In most cases, though, comments will be preserved.\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-comprehensions.allow-dict-calls-with-keyword-arguments`\0A", align 1
