@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1113 = private unnamed_addr constant [1191 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the order of Model's inner classes, methods, and fields as per\0Athe [Django Style Guide].\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe [Django Style Guide] specifies that the order of Model inner classes,\0Aattributes and methods should be as follows:\0A\0A1. All database fields\0A2. Custom manager attributes\0A3. `class Meta`\0A4. `def __str__()`\0A5. `def save()`\0A6. `def get_absolute_url()`\0A7. Any custom methods\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom django.db import models\0A\0A\0Aclass StrBeforeFieldModel(models.Model):\0A    class Meta:\0A        verbose_name = \22test\22\0A        verbose_name_plural = \22tests\22\0A\0A    def __str__(self):\0A        return \22foobar\22\0A\0A    first_name = models.CharField(max_length=32)\0A    last_name = models.CharField(max_length=40)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom django.db import models\0A\0A\0Aclass StrBeforeFieldModel(models.Model):\0A    first_name = models.CharField(max_length=32)\0A    last_name = models.CharField(max_length=40)\0A\0A    class Meta:\0A        verbose_name = \22test\22\0A        verbose_name_plural = \22tests\22\0A\0A    def __str__(self):\0A        return \22foobar\22\0A```\0A\0A[Django Style Guide]: https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/dev/internals/contributing/writing-code/coding-style/#model-style\0A", align 1
