@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1184 = private unnamed_addr constant [764 x i8] c"## What it does\0ACheck for environment variables that are not capitalized.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ABy convention, environment variables should be capitalized.\0A\0AOn Windows, environment variables are case-insensitive and are converted to\0Auppercase, so using lowercase environment variables can lead to subtle bugs.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport os\0A\0Aos.environ[\22foo\22]\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport os\0A\0Aos.environ[\22FOO\22]\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0A\0AThis fix is always marked as unsafe because automatically capitalizing environment variable names\0Acan change program behavior in environments where the variable names are case-sensitive, such as most\0AUnix-like systems.\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `os.environ`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/os.html#os.environ)\0A", align 1
