@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1192 = private unnamed_addr constant [494 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `dict.get()` calls that pass `None` as the default value.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`None` is the default value for `dict.get()`, so it is redundant to pass it\0Aexplicitly.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aages = {\22Tom\22: 23, \22Maria\22: 23, \22Dog\22: 11}\0Aage = ages.get(\22Cat\22, None)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aages = {\22Tom\22: 23, \22Maria\22: 23, \22Dog\22: 11}\0Aage = ages.get(\22Cat\22)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `dict.get`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#dict.get)\0A", align 1
