@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1214 = private unnamed_addr constant [17 x i8] c"quoted-type-alias", align 1
@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1215 = private unnamed_addr constant [2333 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for unnecessary quotes in [PEP 613] explicit type aliases\0Aand [PEP 695] type statements.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AUnnecessary string forward references can lead to additional overhead\0Ain runtime libraries making use of type hints. They can also have bad\0Ainteractions with other runtime uses like [PEP 604] type unions.\0A\0APEP-613 type aliases are only flagged by the rule if Ruff can have high\0Aconfidence that the quotes are unnecessary. Specifically, any PEP-613\0Atype alias where the type expression on the right-hand side contains\0Asubscripts or attribute accesses will not be flagged. This is because\0Atype aliases can reference types that are, for example, generic in stub\0Afiles but not at runtime. That can mean that a type checker expects the\0Areferenced type to be subscripted with type arguments despite the fact\0Athat doing so would fail at runtime if the type alias value was not\0Aquoted. Similarly, a type alias might need to reference a module-level\0Aattribute that exists in a stub file but not at runtime, meaning that\0Athe type alias value would need to be quoted to avoid a runtime error.\0A\0A## Example\0AGiven:\0A```python\0AOptInt: TypeAlias = \22int | None\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0AOptInt: TypeAlias = int | None\0A```\0A\0AGiven:\0A```python\0Atype OptInt = \22int | None\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Atype OptInt = int | None\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThis rule's fix is marked as safe, unless the type annotation contains comments.\0A\0A## See also\0AThis rule only applies to type aliases in non-stub files. For removing quotes in other\0Acontexts or in stub files, see:\0A\0A- [`quoted-annotation-in-stub`][PYI020]: A rule that\0A  removes all quoted annotations from stub files\0A- [`quoted-annotation`][UP037]: A rule that removes unnecessary quotes\0A  from *annotations* in runtime files.\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 613 \E2\80\93 Explicit Type Aliases](https://peps.python.org/pep-0613/)\0A- [PEP 695: Generic Type Alias](https://peps.python.org/pep-0695/#generic-type-alias)\0A- [PEP 604 \E2\80\93 Allow writing union types as `X | Y`](https://peps.python.org/pep-0604/)\0A\0A[PEP 604]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0604/\0A[PEP 613]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0613/\0A[PEP 695]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0695/#generic-type-alias\0A[PYI020]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/quoted-annotation-in-stub/\0A[UP037]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/quoted-annotation/\0A", align 1
