@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1258 = private unnamed_addr constant [505 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `assert` statements that use non-empty tuples as test\0Aconditions.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ANon-empty tuples are always `True`, so an `assert` statement with a\0Anon-empty tuple as its test condition will always pass. This is likely a\0Amistake.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aassert (some_condition,)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aassert some_condition\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: The `assert` statement](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/simple_stmts.html#the-assert-statement)\0A", align 1
