@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1268 = private unnamed_addr constant [609 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for import bindings that are shadowed by loop variables.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AShadowing an import with loop variables makes the code harder to read and\0Areason about, as the identify of the imported binding is no longer clear.\0AIt's also often indicative of a mistake, as it's unlikely that the loop\0Avariable is intended to be used as the imported binding.\0A\0AConsider using a different name for the loop variable.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom os import path\0A\0Afor path in files:\0A    print(path)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom os import path\0A\0A\0Afor filename in files:\0A    print(filename)\0A```\0A", align 1
