@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1283 = private unnamed_addr constant [625 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `__future__` imports that are not located at the beginning of a\0Afile.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AImports from `__future__` must be placed the beginning of the file, before any\0Aother statements (apart from docstrings). The use of `__future__` imports\0Aelsewhere is invalid and will result in a `SyntaxError`.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom pathlib import Path\0A\0Afrom __future__ import annotations\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom __future__ import annotations\0A\0Afrom pathlib import Path\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: Future statements](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/simple_stmts.html#future)\0A", align 1
