22, \22f\22,  # a second  comment\0A]\0A```\0A\0AOther than this, the rule's fix is marked as always being safe, in that\0Ait should very rarely alter the semantics of any Python code.\0AHowever, note that (although it's rare) the value of `__all__`\0Acould be read by code elsewhere that depends on the exact\0Aiteration order of the items in `__all__`, in which case this\0Arule's fix could theoretically cause breakage.\0A", align 1
